# Define common words with reduced weights
[common] -> ;
[common] :- i, me, my, myself, we, our, ours, ourselves, you, your, yours, yourself, yourselves, he, him, his, himself, she, her, hers, herself, it, its, itself, they, them, their, theirs, themselves, what, which, who, whom, this, that, these, those, am, is, are, was, were, be, been, being, have, has, had, having, do, does, did, doing, will, would, shall, should, can, could, may, might, must, ought, i'm, you're, he's, she's, it's, we're, they're, i've, you've, we've, they've, i'd, you'd, he'd, she'd, we'd, they'd, i'll, you'll, he'll, she'll, we'll, they'll, isn't, aren't, wasn't, weren't, hasn't, haven't, hadn't, doesn't, don't, didn't, won't, wouldn't, shan't, shouldn't, can't, cannot, couldn't, mustn't, let's, that's, who's, what's, here's, there's, when's, where's, why's, how's, a, an, the, and, but, if, or, because, as, until, while, since, though, although, of, at, by, for, with, about, against, between, into, through, during, before, after, above, below, to, from, up, down, in, out, on, off, over, under, beside, near, around, again, further, then, once, now, just, still, here, there, when, where, why, how, all, any, both, each, few, more, most, other, some, such, no, nor, not, only, own, same, so, than, too, very, just, quite, really;

# Boost engineering vocabulary that tends to carry the intent of a query.
# Extend this list with terms that matter for your own content.
[important] -> [important]!250;
[important] :- reliability, perf, scale, diff, review, release, deployment, revert, abort, metrics, configs, version;

# Phrase boosting: an exact multi-word match outranks the same words scattered
# across a document. Add your own phrases in this form.
first principles -> first principles!300;

@default  # Apply this rule base to all queries by default